Z||000005||KRMFiero||08-16-2001||10:42 AM||||Oh yea you would have to drill new holes for starter also...  Do a Seach for umm:<P>RWD 2.8<BR>RWD 3.4    (People use RWD 3.4's see what they do, blocks are pretty much the same)<BR>S-10 2.8<P>things like that...||||reg||1
Z||000006||swoods||08-16-2001||10:53 AM||||Aright has any body done this before please help send info Ive tried everting to find more info but very little help.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Indiana_resto_guy||08-16-2001||10:58 AM||||The only othe 2.8 block that will work is a 'W' block. All the others have the starter on the wrong side and the other side cannot be drilled for a starter as the oil filter would then be in the way of the starter.<BR>Find something in a front wheel drive like a Berretta, Corsica, Cutlass ect.||||reg||1
Z||000008||swoods||08-16-2001||11:08 AM||||Well I found that 2.8 s-10 motor and it has all brand new parts the parts are high quality. I really was hoping the motor would work but it looks like itll be alot of work. So what Im wondering is can I use all the new parts inside the motor And just rebuild my 2.8 with them.||||reg||1
Z||000009||isthiswhereiputausername?||08-16-2001||12:06 PM||||you could switch "some" stuff over.. you might be better off selling that block/complete motor and using the money to rebuild yours..<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Indiana_resto_guy||08-16-2001||04:20 PM||||*<p>[This message has been edited by Indiana_resto_guy (edited 08-16-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||Indiana_resto_guy||08-16-2001||04:21 PM||||You can 'swap' the guts from one to the other providing you block is in good condition and does not need to be bored. Make sure that you hone the cylinders out and a new set of rings should be in order.<BR>You can save the heads off the 'doner' motor as well, they are the same head.<BR>If you do this, get a high volumn oil pump to install as well and check the timing chain (I would put in a new one anyway).||||reg||1
Z||000012||swoods||08-17-2001||01:26 AM||||The 2.8 in the s-10 is totally build up with performance trw parts and a few diffrent other parts. Thats the only reason I was thinking about this motor.||||reg||1
